# Exodiff spec for the melt-only case (materials_mechanical_melt.yaml).
#
# Same tolerances as denudation.exodiff -- the two runs share a mesh, a thermal
# subdomain and an output layout. The fields that matter here are the discrete
# ones. In top_block (the "IceWedge" material, melt active) failure_modes is 0 or
# 32 (bit 0x20, melt) and nothing else, failure_state is 0 or 800000 (8 points x
# the melt magnitude 1e5), and cell_death matches the fully-thawed set exactly.
# In bottom_block (the "Permafrost" material, which omits the melt key) both stay
# 0 no matter how far it thaws. Those are integer-valued, so any change in the
# melt criterion, or a regression of the per-block material dispatch of GitHub
# #121, shows up as a relative difference of 1.0, far above the tolerance.
#
COORDINATES absolute 1.e-6

TIME STEPS relative 1.e-6 floor 0.0

# Tolerances are sized to absorb cross-build / parallel reduction-order
# noise while still catching real regressions. The engineering quantities
# are checked RELATIVE; the near-zero kinematic fields (velocity,
# acceleration), which are physically ~0 in this slow-erosion problem, are
# checked ABSOLUTE with a small floor. Displacements -- the meaningful
# mechanical response -- stay at relative 2e-5. (Dead-node velocity and
# acceleration are zeroed by the solver, so the gold and any build agree
# exactly there.)
NODAL VARIABLES relative 2.0e-5 floor 1.0e-5
	temperature        relative 6.0e-6 floor 1.0e-12
	temperature_dot    relative 6.0e-6 floor 1.0e-12
	displacement_x
	displacement_y
	displacement_z
	velocity_x               absolute 1.0e-4 floor 1.0e-6
	velocity_y               absolute 1.0e-4 floor 1.0e-6
	velocity_z               absolute 1.0e-4 floor 1.0e-6
	acceleration_x           absolute 1.0e-5 floor 1.0e-6
	acceleration_y           absolute 1.0e-5 floor 1.0e-6
	acceleration_z           absolute 1.0e-5 floor 1.0e-6
	displacement_residual_x  absolute 1.0e-5 floor 1.0e-6
	displacement_residual_y  absolute 1.0e-5 floor 1.0e-6
	displacement_residual_z  absolute 1.0e-5 floor 1.0e-6
	proj_nodal_linear        absolute 1.0e-12 floor 1.0e-12

# Element quantities (Cauchy_Stress ~ O(1e4), eqps, plastic strain, failure
# state/modes) are checked relative. The large stresses agree to ~1e-8, but
# small-magnitude stress components drift up to ~6e-5 across compilers, so the
# relative tolerance is 2e-4. The floor drops near-zero shear-stress noise
# (~1e-7) without masking a changed failure mode (a flipped 0->bit is rel
# diff 1.0).
ELEMENT VARIABLES relative 2.0e-4 floor 1.0e-3
